  "implementation": [
    "Distinct AppExecution OSObject owns real frozen GPU/GMU providers/descriptors,actual RegisterMaps/Ring,IOUserClient,opening task and immutable authority code/storage owner",
    "Actual Maps->AppExecution factory and private Ring prepare/check/close chain. No kernel-client callback casts or fallback;all three independent application acquire/check/release callbacks mandatory",
    "Current opening task reference and actual provider/client MACF/filter checks precede foreign app acquire. Original XNU post-open checks remain required;early subset is not a full entitlement/open replacement",
    "Acquire/check/close phases serialize foreign callbacks without holding owner lock/domain gate/issuer. Callback reentry/pending-state rejects,unknown acquire/check/release retains references without reset/retry",
    "Each check takes actual calling-task reference and calls independent real authority again;no cached raw0 accepted as later access permission",
    "Only real release callback success returns held task/client/code/provider/descriptor/map/ring references and drops self-pin;kernel/app session preparation excludes overlap including kernel acquire-in-progress"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "NO concrete hardware application-authority callback implementation is supplied or selected here;this object consumes a mandatory real backend. Missing callbacks reject before creation;no fake success",
    "Application IOService/IOUserClient frontend and application OOB/private VM/submit binding remain unconnected;existing public endpoint is kernel-only",
    "Current app close entry has not exposed native app work. Future actual application OOB/VM/submit teardown must precede permission-owner release;never treat an empty CPU list as DMA-stop proof",
    "Task/metadata/software policy and prior kernel test results do not establish app hardware rights",
    "No acquire/check/release/MACF/IOKit/native/GPU or phone executed;host compiler/linker and actual-file original-loader parser only"
  ],
